Hello all.

Heinz just asked me to announce the LVM kernel patch against
the new 2.3.9 kernel.

Changes:
 - Support for Kernel 2.3.9
 - Source code cleaned up to remove KERNEL_VERSION conditional code

[The kernel patch is tagged as version 0.7 but it is fully compatible
with the current 0.6 user mode tools.]


The patch is available for download at
ftp://linux.msede.com/lvm/v0.6/patch-2.3.9-LVM.gz

A list of available mirror sites (which may not have synced yet) 
is available at the LVM web page at
http://linux.msede.com/lvm/


Enjoy.
Michael

